00:41:19.202 --> 00:41:20.501
Get a drink or something.


00:41:25.041 --> 00:41:28.275
Hey slow down, you're gonna
give me a heart attack.


00:41:28.277 --> 00:41:31.078
That girl, she gave me this.


00:41:33.716 --> 00:41:34.749
What does it say?


00:41:39.422 --> 00:41:40.321
Oh, God.


00:41:46.396 --> 00:41:48.662
So that was handed to us


00:41:48.664 --> 00:41:50.331
by someone who lives here.


00:41:57.573 --> 00:42:01.042
I can't be responsible
for everyone's happiness.


00:42:01.044 --> 00:42:03.144
They all have to
responsible for their own.


00:42:03.146 --> 00:42:05.413
I understand that but
why do you think someone


00:42:05.415 --> 00:42:07.681
would feel they needed help?


00:42:07.683 --> 00:42:09.083
Who knows?


00:42:09.085 --> 00:42:10.418
All I know is one bad apple


00:42:10.420 --> 00:42:12.653
does not make for
a rotten barrel.


00:42:12.655 --> 00:42:14.722
But it's not just one Reverend.


00:42:14.724 --> 00:42:17.591
We spoke to others, we
showed them the note.


00:42:17.593 --> 00:42:19.126
When they saw someone
had broken rank


00:42:19.128 --> 00:42:21.562
they also indicated
they were unhappy.


00:42:23.132 --> 00:42:25.332
We have few people out there
that would like to leave.


00:42:28.805 --> 00:42:31.539
People play games, friend.


00:42:31.541 --> 00:42:34.075
They play games and they lie.


00:42:34.077 --> 00:42:37.511
Are you suggesting that
the people who wanna leave


00:42:37.513 --> 00:42:40.347
are lying about the abuses here?


00:42:41.551 --> 00:42:43.651
People are unhappy
and they play games.


00:42:43.653 --> 00:42:45.352
I can't be responsible for that.


00:42:46.489 --> 00:42:47.788
Now just go.


00:42:47.790 --> 00:42:50.124
Leave us in peace.


00:42:50.126 --> 00:42:53.494
So if we take those who
are unhappy back with us,


00:42:53.496 --> 00:42:55.296
back to American,
you don't object.


00:43:01.838 --> 00:43:05.673
If they want to go, they can go.


00:43:16.886 --> 00:43:18.319
You're really leaving?


00:43:19.655 --> 00:43:21.155
Quite a few people are.


00:43:24.127 --> 00:43:25.326
Why don't you come with us?


00:43:25.328 --> 00:43:26.560
This is my home.


00:43:26.562 --> 00:43:28.662
You're home is back
in San Francisco.


00:43:28.664 --> 00:43:29.563
Not anymore.


00:43:31.834 --> 00:43:33.734
He really has a hold
on you, doesn't he?


00:43:33.736 --> 00:43:35.336
I still believe in the message.


00:43:35.338 --> 00:43:36.337
What message is that?


00:43:36.339 --> 00:43:37.238
Love.


00:43:39.509 --> 00:43:41.675
It was about love
in the beginning


00:43:41.677 --> 00:43:43.644
now it's all about fear.


00:43:43.646 --> 00:43:46.614
There's as many guns as
people here these days.


00:43:46.616 --> 00:43:48.182
Things have really changed.


00:43:48.184 --> 00:43:49.850
I'm sorry you feel that way.


00:43:50.653 --> 00:43:52.153
Why can't you see it.


00:43:52.155 --> 00:43:52.887
See what?


00:43:52.889 --> 00:43:55.789
The Reverend is a paranoid mess.


00:43:55.791 --> 00:43:57.791
He's leading us all
down a dark path.


00:43:57.793 --> 00:43:59.793
All I know is I've
seen the Reverend


00:43:59.795 --> 00:44:02.396
perform miracles
year after year.


00:44:02.398 --> 00:44:05.199
He's healed the blind,
helped the crippled walk.


00:44:05.201 --> 00:44:07.668
He's clearly been chosen by God.


00:44:07.670 --> 00:44:10.337
Who are we to
question the anointed?


00:44:15.811 --> 00:44:17.645
Love you.


00:44:35.731 --> 00:44:38.666
Congressman,
Congressman, Congressman,


00:44:38.668 --> 00:44:40.568
take me with you, please.


00:44:42.572 --> 00:44:43.671
You wanna leave?


00:44:44.807 --> 00:44:46.340
I haven't had the
courage to say anything


00:44:46.342 --> 00:44:48.892
but I feel like I finally can.


00:44:48.894 --> 00:44:51.445
You seemed pretty committed
to Jim Jones just an hour ago.


00:44:51.447 --> 00:44:53.447
I'm one of his highest deputies


00:44:53.449 --> 00:44:54.648
if I hadn't helped
him keep people out


00:44:54.650 --> 00:44:55.683
he would've hurt me.


00:44:55.685 --> 00:44:57.785
But the Reverend
has lost his way


00:44:57.787 --> 00:44:58.953
and I can't be held responsible


00:44:58.955 --> 00:45:00.721
for what happens here anymore.


00:45:00.723 --> 00:45:02.856
I just wanna be my own man.


00:45:02.858 --> 00:45:03.824
He's lying.


00:45:03.826 --> 00:45:05.793
Yeah, he's still loyal to Jones.


00:45:05.795 --> 00:45:09.797
Guys, I've done things to hurt
you and I've made mistakes


00:45:09.799 --> 00:45:12.733
but I just wanna be free
like the rest of you.


00:45:12.735 --> 00:45:14.435
That's bullshit.


00:45:14.437 --> 00:45:17.838
All right, all right, let's
everybody stay calm here.


00:45:19.642 --> 00:45:22.409
Now if you're sincere about
your desire to leave this place


00:45:22.411 --> 00:45:24.745
- then what I can do is...
- Swear to God,


00:45:24.747 --> 00:45:26.513
I'm telling the truth.


00:45:26.515 --> 00:45:27.648
I just wanna leave.


00:45:29.819 --> 00:45:30.718
Okay.


00:45:31.787 --> 00:45:33.354
Then you can come with us.


00:45:33.990 --> 00:45:34.888
Come on.


00:45:46.636 --> 00:45:48.802
You know, I don't know.


00:45:48.804 --> 00:45:53.274
Listen, I just, I don't
know why you would turn.


00:45:53.276 --> 00:45:54.842
You know it's a lie
and you know it's fake.


00:45:54.844 --> 00:45:55.743
The Congressman...


00:45:57.446 --> 00:45:59.947
Our plane, where is it?


00:45:59.949 --> 00:46:01.815
I'm told fuel was low.


00:46:01.817 --> 00:46:03.017
The pilot's gone to
a base the other side


00:46:03.019 --> 00:46:04.652
of Georgetown to fill up.


00:46:04.654 --> 00:46:07.554
And how long are we expected
to wait for this plane?


00:46:07.556 --> 00:46:09.690
Well, I've given
ETA of 5:00 p.m.


00:46:09.692 --> 00:46:11.392
Only a half an hour away.


00:46:11.394 --> 00:46:14.328
There's a waiting room
over in the main building.


00:46:14.330 --> 00:46:15.729
I suggest we wait in there.


00:46:20.569 --> 00:46:21.468
Fine.


00:46:34.317 --> 00:46:35.082
Where's Snyder?


00:46:44.894 --> 00:46:46.794
Oh, Christ.


00:46:55.037 --> 00:46:58.939
Please, we can settle this
with a simple discussion.


00:47:08.551 --> 00:47:09.850
It doesn't have to be like this.


00:47:09.852 --> 00:47:11.952
It's too late for that.


00:47:38.848 --> 00:47:40.981
It's far, far harder
to have walked


00:47:40.983 --> 00:47:43.050
through every day, die slowly,


00:47:43.986 --> 00:47:45.652
and from the time you're a child


00:47:45.654 --> 00:47:47.621
to the time you get
gray, you're dying.


00:47:48.824 --> 00:47:50.858
It as a revolutionary suicide,


00:47:50.860 --> 00:47:53.894
this is not
self-destructive suicide.


00:47:53.896 --> 00:47:56.864
So they'll pay for this,
they brought this upon us


00:47:56.866 --> 00:47:58.766
and they'll pay for that.


00:47:58.768 --> 00:48:00.567
I leave that destiny to them.


00:48:02.438 --> 00:48:05.806
1,000 people who said, "We
don't like the way the world is


00:48:05.808 --> 00:48:07.174
"take our life from us."


00:48:07.176 --> 00:48:10.511
"We laid it down, we got tired."


00:48:10.513 --> 00:48:11.979
"We didn't commit suicide,


00:48:11.981 --> 00:48:14.715
"we committed an act of
revolutionary suicide


00:48:14.717 --> 00:48:17.985
"protesting the condition
of an inhumane world."


00:49:01.096 --> 00:49:05.833
And he took the bread,
gave thanks, and broke it.


00:49:05.835 --> 00:49:11.104
He gave it them saying, "This
is my body given for you,


00:49:11.106 --> 00:49:14.775
"do this in remembrance of me."


00:49:20.082 --> 00:49:22.115
Take it my lovechild.


00:49:22.117 --> 00:49:24.017
Only by tasting
the body of Christ


00:49:24.019 --> 00:49:25.919
will you find your answers.


00:49:34.964 --> 00:49:37.798
In the same way he took the cup


00:49:39.969 --> 00:49:43.871
and said, "This cup is the
new covenant in my blood,


00:49:45.040 --> 00:49:46.673
"which is poured out for you."


00:52:48.691 --> 00:52:49.389
Hello.


00:52:50.325 --> 00:52:52.192
I'm so sorry the door was open.


00:52:52.194 --> 00:52:53.727
Oh no, that's okay.


00:52:53.729 --> 00:52:55.762
I was just taking a walk.


00:52:55.764 --> 00:52:57.230
My name's Gaia.


00:52:57.232 --> 00:52:59.332
Yeah, I'm really
sorry to bother you.


00:52:59.334 --> 00:53:00.333
Wait.


00:53:02.871 --> 00:53:04.471
I can see you're tired.


00:53:04.473 --> 00:53:06.139
You're welcome to rest here.


00:53:11.914 --> 00:53:14.948
I didn't expect to meet
an American out here.


00:53:14.950 --> 00:53:17.250
I came to Guyana four years ago.


00:53:17.252 --> 00:53:19.186
My husband worked here.


00:53:19.188 --> 00:53:20.454
He passed away.


00:53:20.456 --> 00:53:21.321
I'm so sorry.


00:53:23.325 --> 00:53:26.259
I grieved for such a long time,


00:53:26.261 --> 00:53:29.863
constantly reliving the
same moments day after day


00:53:30.499 --> 00:53:32.299
then something happened,


00:53:33.769 --> 00:53:35.335
I moved beyond all that.


00:53:38.006 --> 00:53:39.206
I woke up.


00:53:39.208 --> 00:53:40.474
What happened?


00:53:40.476 --> 00:53:42.909
It takes effort
to be effortless.


00:53:44.847 --> 00:53:47.914
And sometimes you have
to go through the pain


00:53:47.916 --> 00:53:49.316
for it to become painless.


00:53:50.385 --> 00:53:52.219
The process can be frustrating.


00:53:53.889 --> 00:53:55.455
I was part of the
People's Temple.


00:53:55.457 --> 00:53:59.292
We were church commune who
lived near by back in the 70s.


00:53:59.294 --> 00:54:00.961
Jonestown.


00:54:00.963 --> 00:54:02.129
Yeah.


00:54:02.131 --> 00:54:03.997
A very sad thing.


00:54:06.168 --> 00:54:09.136
I survived it but it's
hunted me ever since.


00:54:10.205 --> 00:54:11.438
I came back out
here hoping to deal


00:54:11.440 --> 00:54:13.373
with my feelings
about what happened.


00:54:16.545 --> 00:54:19.312
I'm so conflicted
because I wanna connect


00:54:19.314 --> 00:54:21.348
with something spiritual,


00:54:21.350 --> 00:54:24.184
something beyond
everyday existence


00:54:25.287 --> 00:54:26.553
but to connect to that


00:54:26.555 --> 00:54:28.955
should make you feel
free not imprisoned.


00:54:30.959 --> 00:54:32.826
That's how I felt
within the church.


00:54:34.229 --> 00:54:36.163
I thought it would open
my mind and my heart


00:54:36.165 --> 00:54:37.964
but all it did was
close them off.


00:54:41.403 --> 00:54:45.372
You know, religion doesn't have
a monopoly on spirituality.


00:54:45.374 --> 00:54:50.310
And your feelings aren't
subjugated by not knowing.


00:54:50.312 --> 00:54:54.981
We are all connected, you
just don't see it yet.


00:54:57.252 --> 00:55:02.222
Sometimes it takes an event
so incredible to wake us up


00:55:02.224 --> 00:55:06.359
for better or worse and
you don't get to choose.


00:55:36.391 --> 00:55:41.194
I'm constantly amazed every
time I walk through here.


00:55:41.196 --> 00:55:42.429
It's so beautiful.


00:55:42.431 --> 00:55:46.499
Nothing is more perfect
than this moment.


00:55:46.501 --> 00:55:47.367
Don't you agree?


00:55:49.338 --> 00:55:50.403
Wake up, Sarah.


00:55:51.506 --> 00:55:53.206
I am awake.


00:55:53.208 --> 00:55:55.475
Oh, there pick those.


00:55:55.477 --> 00:55:57.444
They're good for bug bites.


00:55:57.446 --> 00:55:59.913
Just a few, save
some for next time.


00:56:04.152 --> 00:56:07.587
Each expression of
life on this planet


00:56:07.589 --> 00:56:10.423
has its own unique vibration.


00:56:18.066 --> 00:56:21.368
Connection to every living
thing is available to us


00:56:21.370 --> 00:56:23.937
if we're willing
to be open to it.


00:56:23.939 --> 00:56:25.171
I want to be open to it


00:56:25.173 --> 00:56:27.407
but I just feel so disconnected.


00:56:27.409 --> 00:56:32.612
You're still a willing
partner in this dance of life


00:56:32.614 --> 00:56:34.514
whether you
acknowledge it or not.


00:56:34.516 --> 00:56:36.283
I have moments where
I feel connected


00:56:36.285 --> 00:56:39.286
but I can't sustain it.


00:56:39.288 --> 00:56:41.121
It feels like
there's resistance.


00:56:43.392 --> 00:56:46.092
Start with the body and
the mind will follow.


00:56:55.470 --> 00:56:57.637
We've all had
trauma in our lives


00:56:57.639 --> 00:57:00.540
it doesn't lessen what
you've been through


00:57:00.542 --> 00:57:02.375
just that you're not defined


00:57:02.377 --> 00:57:05.211
by your past, good
or not so good.


00:57:06.381 --> 00:57:08.381
It's human to feel emotions


00:57:08.383 --> 00:57:11.418
but people think they
are their emotions


00:57:11.420 --> 00:57:14.521
when it's really just
one small part of us


00:57:14.523 --> 00:57:18.525
yet we let those emotions
control our lives.


00:57:18.527 --> 00:57:21.594
So how do we break
free of those emotions?


00:57:21.596 --> 00:57:26.466
First acknowledge that you
can feel, let yourself feel


00:57:26.468 --> 00:57:29.202
but then remember that
you're not your thoughts


00:57:29.204 --> 00:57:31.504
nor your emotions.


00:57:31.506 --> 00:57:33.473
Sounds so simple.


00:57:33.475 --> 00:57:38.311
It's never simple to undo
decades of damaging thoughts.


00:57:38.313 --> 00:57:41.448
It takes a great deal of belief.


00:57:41.450 --> 00:57:44.451
I did believe in something
look where that go me.


00:57:44.453 --> 00:57:48.488
But have you ever believed in
yourself, believed in Sarah?


00:57:48.490 --> 00:57:51.157
I know it's hard for
you to believe me


00:57:51.159 --> 00:57:54.260
but when a person allows
their emotional state


00:57:54.262 --> 00:57:56.663
to overcloud their judgment


00:57:56.665 --> 00:58:00.000
it makes it difficult
to really see.


00:58:00.002 --> 00:58:01.601
Can't say my emotional state


00:58:01.603 --> 00:58:03.203
is in great shape right now.


00:58:04.306 --> 00:58:06.072
Have you tried meditation?


00:58:06.074 --> 00:58:09.743
Kind of, I found it
hard to quieten my mind.


00:58:09.745 --> 00:58:12.379
The negative thoughts
just kept coming.


00:58:16.651 --> 00:58:18.218
What's this?


00:58:18.220 --> 00:58:20.620
If you can't change
your thinking on your own


00:58:20.622 --> 00:58:22.122
this will help.


00:58:22.124 --> 00:58:23.023
What is it?


00:58:24.559 --> 00:58:27.127
It's an ancient mixture
I learned to make


00:58:27.129 --> 00:58:29.763
from the locals
here, very powerful.


00:58:29.765 --> 00:58:34.067
It induces a state of
relaxation and centeredness.


00:58:35.170 --> 00:58:37.537
Drink this and we'll
meditate together.


00:58:37.539 --> 00:58:42.308
This and the meditation will
allow your mind to expand.


00:58:42.310 --> 00:58:46.046
You'll see reality for
the way it really is.


00:58:47.149 --> 00:58:49.282
I'm not sure
I wanna drink it.


00:58:49.284 --> 00:58:50.617
What are you afraid of?


00:58:52.521 --> 00:58:55.155
Being out of control, I guess.


00:58:55.157 --> 00:58:57.590
How has your life
been, being in control?


00:58:59.594 --> 00:59:00.460
Not so good.


00:59:01.797 --> 00:59:03.530
Maybe it's time to surrender.


00:59:14.342 --> 00:59:15.308
Close your eyes.


00:59:20.082 --> 00:59:24.551
Now, begin by becoming
aware of your breathing


00:59:26.088 --> 00:59:32.792
and allow your awareness to
draw down into your body,


00:59:34.629 --> 00:59:39.099
inhaling and exhaling.


00:59:41.503 --> 00:59:48.842
Inhale, allow the breath
to enter the nostrils


00:59:48.844 --> 00:59:51.611
cooling the nasal passages.


00:59:51.613 --> 00:59:55.415
As it goes and touches
the back of your throat


00:59:56.718 --> 01:00:01.688
and draws down, deep into
the bottom of your lungs.


01:00:03.525 --> 01:00:05.758
The breath is your guide.


01:00:07.395 --> 01:00:10.730
The breath is your refuge.


01:00:12.801 --> 01:00:16.336
As thoughts arise,
which they will,


01:00:17.672 --> 01:00:22.342
gently bring your attention
back to your breath,


01:00:23.879 --> 01:00:26.746
inhaling and exhaling.


01:00:28.250 --> 01:00:32.585
Deeper and deeper.


01:00:59.614 --> 01:01:03.816
You know your
life is just a dream, don't you?


01:01:27.375 --> 01:01:29.342
<i> They took</i>
<i>us and put us in chains</i>


01:01:29.344 --> 01:01:32.278
<i>and that's nothing, this
business, that business,</i>


01:01:32.280 --> 01:01:33.980
<i>there's no comparison
to that, to this.</i>


01:01:35.383 --> 01:01:36.616
<i>They robbed us of our land,</i>


01:01:36.618 --> 01:01:37.684
<i>and they've taken
us and driven us</i>


01:01:37.686 --> 01:01:39.652
<i>and we tried to find ourselves.</i>


01:01:39.654 --> 01:01:42.222
<i>We tried to find a new
beginning but it's too late.</i>


01:01:42.224 --> 01:01:43.723
<i>You can't separate yourself</i>


01:01:43.725 --> 01:01:46.526
<i>from your brother and
your sister.</i>


01:01:46.528 --> 01:01:47.660
<i>No way I'm gonna do it.</i>


01:01:47.662 --> 01:01:48.628
<i>I refuse.</i>


01:01:48.630 --> 01:01:50.162
<i>I don't know who fired the shot,</i>


01:01:50.164 --> 01:01:51.697
<i>I don't know who
killed the congressman</i>


01:01:51.700 --> 01:01:53.666
<i>but as far as I'm
concerned I killed him.</i>


01:01:53.668 --> 01:01:56.803
<i>With respect, die with
a degree of dignity.</i>


01:01:56.805 --> 01:01:58.220
It's done.


01:01:58.222 --> 01:01:59.638
<i>Lay down your
life with dignity.</i>


01:01:59.641 --> 01:02:00.789
Good.


01:02:00.791 --> 01:02:01.940
<i>Don't lay down
with tears and agony.</i>


01:02:01.943 --> 01:02:04.644
You have the documents?


01:02:04.646 --> 01:02:06.646
In the box over there.


01:02:06.648 --> 01:02:09.449
<i>Don't, don't be this way.</i>


01:02:09.451 --> 01:02:10.350
Okay.


01:02:11.753 --> 01:02:13.502
<i>This is not
the way for people</i>


01:02:13.504 --> 01:02:15.254
<i>who are Socialists
or Communists to die.</i>


01:02:17.892 --> 01:02:18.925
<i>No way for us to die.</i>


01:02:18.927 --> 01:02:21.027
<i>We must die with some dignity.</i>


01:02:25.000 --> 01:02:28.835
<i>Mother, mother, mother,
mother, mother please.</i>


01:02:31.372 --> 01:02:33.906
<i>Please, please, please don't
do this, don't do this.</i>


01:02:36.578 --> 01:02:39.345
<i>Lay down your life with your
child but don't do this.</i>


01:02:48.590 --> 01:02:51.057
This is Snyder.
Operation MK Guyana


01:02:51.059 --> 01:02:52.792
is now terminated officially.


01:02:54.396 --> 01:02:56.696
Send in the crew, I'll
be on the next flight.


01:03:02.904 --> 01:03:05.705
<i>No, no, sorrow
that it's all over.</i>


01:03:05.707 --> 01:03:08.574
<i>I'm glad it's over.</i>


01:03:12.947 --> 01:03:14.447
What was in that drink?


01:03:14.449 --> 01:03:15.815
Water.


01:03:15.817 --> 01:03:16.649
What?


01:03:16.651 --> 01:03:18.384
It was just water.


01:03:18.386 --> 01:03:19.619
No, but I saw...


01:03:19.621 --> 01:03:21.854
Yes, you saw.


01:03:22.957 --> 01:03:24.791
You wanted to awaken
and see the world


01:03:24.793 --> 01:03:26.793
for what it really is.


01:03:26.795 --> 01:03:30.697
You didn't think you could do
it on your own but you did.


01:03:30.699 --> 01:03:32.832
You are powerful.


01:03:32.834 --> 01:03:34.734
You just proved it.


01:03:34.736 --> 01:03:37.804
There was nothing in
that vile but water.


01:03:37.806 --> 01:03:40.673
But I saw something,
a past incident


01:03:40.675 --> 01:03:41.641
that I wasn't present at.


01:03:41.643 --> 01:03:43.543
How could I have seen that?


01:03:43.545 --> 01:03:45.578
When your third eye is opened


01:03:45.580 --> 01:03:47.947
you're capable of
seeing everything.


01:03:53.621 --> 01:03:54.887
What the hell is going on?


01:03:56.558 --> 01:03:58.891
I ask myself the same question.


01:03:58.893 --> 01:04:01.728
The agency assigned
me to watch you.


01:04:01.730 --> 01:04:04.664
Make sure the memories
stayed repressed.


01:04:04.666 --> 01:04:07.400
I thought it would
be an easy gig


01:04:07.402 --> 01:04:09.369
just ushering you
through a few years


01:04:09.371 --> 01:04:10.937
of medication and counseling


01:04:10.939 --> 01:04:12.638
and then passing you
off to the next one


01:04:12.640 --> 01:04:14.507
in line for this shit detail.


01:04:14.509 --> 01:04:18.911
But then you came off the meds


01:04:18.913 --> 01:04:20.680
and psychiatry wasn't
enough anymore.


01:04:20.682 --> 01:04:21.981
Now here we are.


01:04:21.983 --> 01:04:23.149
What the hell are
you talking about?


01:04:23.151 --> 01:04:24.417
What agency?


01:04:24.419 --> 01:04:25.651
That's irrelevant.


01:04:25.653 --> 01:04:28.454
What's important is
that I have fucked up


01:04:28.456 --> 01:04:30.757
and I'm gonna have
to rectify that.


01:04:30.759 --> 01:04:32.158
You think you can just
kill me in cold blood


01:04:32.160 --> 01:04:33.593
and get away with it.


01:04:33.595 --> 01:04:34.427
Think it.


01:04:34.429 --> 01:04:35.728
No, I know it.


01:04:35.730 --> 01:04:37.964
I've handled far
tougher marks than you.


01:04:37.966 --> 01:04:39.699
This is as straight
forward as it gets.


01:04:39.701 --> 01:04:42.902
Mentally ill girl racked
with survivor's guilt


01:04:42.904 --> 01:04:46.038
comes back to the site of the
massacre and commits suicide.


01:04:46.040 --> 01:04:47.640
The headline writes itself.


01:05:37.959 --> 01:05:39.625
Where's the bitch?


01:06:41.556 --> 01:06:43.956
Come to me my lovechild.


01:06:43.958 --> 01:06:45.791
You belong with us.


01:06:56.971 --> 01:07:00.172
You've taken up space in my
head for over a decade now.


01:07:01.809 --> 01:07:04.076
Consider this your
eviction notice.


01:07:05.547 --> 01:07:07.580
I'm taking back my power.


01:07:09.017 --> 01:07:10.917
I will no longer live in fear.


01:07:12.687 --> 01:07:14.820
You're nothing to me now.


01:07:56.898 --> 01:08:01.000
The battle is on for
your heart and your mind.


01:08:01.002 --> 01:08:03.135
So don't give them
over so readily.


01:08:05.073 --> 01:08:08.808
Don't buy into the
phony political races.


01:08:09.844 --> 01:08:12.244
Turn off the manufactured news.


01:08:13.381 --> 01:08:16.215
Reject all of the
fear mongering.


01:08:18.086 --> 01:08:22.121
Go outside, connect with nature.


01:08:23.324 --> 01:08:24.357
Find love.


01:08:26.094 --> 01:08:27.760
Feel gratitude.


01:08:29.731 --> 01:08:33.099
Choose a life where
you don't live in fear.


01:08:34.736 --> 01:08:38.671
Fear is the prison they
want you to live in.


01:08:40.942 --> 01:08:42.341
But what is there to fear?


01:08:44.145 --> 01:08:45.011
Nothing.


01:08:46.748 --> 01:08:48.748
We are all one consciousness


01:08:48.750 --> 01:08:51.150
experiencing itself
subjectively.


01:08:53.121 --> 01:08:56.756
Death doesn't actually exist.


01:08:58.259 --> 01:09:01.260
Our lives are all a dream


01:09:01.262 --> 01:09:07.333
and each of us is the
imagination of ourselves.


01:09:10.171 --> 01:09:12.238
But remember...


01:09:12.240 --> 01:09:19.145
imagination
is evidence of the divine.


